e\":0,\"unit\":\"px\"}}},\"background\":{\"color\":\"rgba(var(--kubio-color-3),1)\"},\"typography\":{\"color\":\"rgba(var(--kubio-color-3-variant-5),1)\",\"weight\":400}}}},\"hash\":\"s5x8-WcE_6\"},\"shortcode\":\"[contact-form-7 id=\\\"42\\\"][/contact-form-7]\",\"formId\":\"42\"} /-->\n<!-- /wp:kubio/column -->\n<!-- /wp:kubio/row -->\n<!-- /wp:kubio/section -->','Home','','inherit','closed','closed','','8-revision-v1','','','2026-05-07 18:09:35','2026-05-07 17:09:35','',8,'http://csilvr.local/?p=169',0,'revision','',0);
INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (171,1,'2026-05-07 18:28:39','2026-05-07 17:28:39','<!-- wp:kubio/section {\"kubio\":{\"styleRef\":\"ts6Q7SiM1t\",\"hash\":\"D8NtOKsYb5\"},\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Section\"},\"anchor\":\"section\"} -->\n<!-- wp:kubio/row {\"kubio\":{\"styleRef\":\"CPwVVCOHY\",\"props\":{\"layout\":{\"itemsPerRow\":1,\"custom\":[{\"type\":\"custom\",\"custom\":{\"value\":100,\"unit\":\"%\"}}],\"equalHeight\":true,\"equalWidth\":false}},\"hash\":\"og010ksIH2\"}} -->\n<!-- wp:kubio/column {\"kubio\":{\"styleRef\":\"Oc0zUKjAuK\",\"_style\":{\"descendants\":{\"container\":{\"columnWidth\":{\"type\":\"custom\",\"custom\":{\"value\":100,\"unit\":\"%\"}}}}},\"hash\":\"X92lzwzIxs\"}} -->\n<!-- wp:kubio/text {\"kubio\":{\"styleRef\":\"XTi94nuhO\",\"hash\":\"oQnuND33w\"}} -->\nProject Overview<br>CSI: LVR (Leeds Virtual Reality Crime Scene Investigation) is an academic team project exploring the use of immersive technologies to support crime scene investigation training. The project aims to model investigative workflows, evidence handling procedures, and decision-making processes within a simulated digital environment.<br>The system is designed to demonstrate how virtual environments can support forensic education by allowing users to observe and analyse a structured crime scene scenario. Through a controlled digital setting, the project highlights key investigative principles such as evidence recognition, procedural sequencing, and scene awareness.<br>Current Implementation<br>The current version of CSI: LVR is implemented as a web-based demonstrator. Rather than a fully immersive virtual reality system, this platform presents a conceptual prototype intended to validate design decisions, system structure, and investigative workflow logic. The demonstrator includes a structures login interface and a visual representation of the crime scene environment.<br>This staged implementation reflects an iterative development approach, prioritising feasibility, accessibility, and conceptual clarity within the available timeframe. While immersive VR interaction remains a potential future direction, the present demonstrator focuses on validating core system concepts before further expansion.<br>Project Scope<br>Virtual crime scene modelling<br>Evidence handling workflow representation<br>Procedural sequencing validation<br>Web-based demonstrator implementation<br>Future immersive VR expansion potential<br>CSI: LVR was developed as part of a university team project, integrating research in virtual reality, 3D modelling, usability, and software engineering.\n<!-- /wp:kubio/text -->\n<!-- /wp:kubio/column -->\n<!-- /wp:kubio/row -->\n<!-- /wp:kubio/section -->','About Project','','inherit','closed','closed','','38-revision-v1','','','2026-05-07 18:28:39','2026-05-07 17:28:39','',38,'http://csilvr.local/?p=171',0,'revision','',0);
